    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I'm ok with the code you're suggesting, although I think it would be interesting to consider doing the code here and avoiding another iteration:\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n    var name = item.path || item.name;\r\n    var hidden = hide.indexOf(name) > -1;\r\n    if (!hidden && reverseOrder[name] !== undefined) {\r\n      orderedFacets[reverseOrder[name]] = item;\r\n    } else if (!hidden) {\r\n      remainingFacets.push(item);\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot sure if it's worth the difference, but the code doesn't look much harder to me, and should be more efficient in theory.\r\n\r\n(obviously this code suggestion requires the other iteration, the utility function and the other conditions to be modified)",
